# configs/ — keep the *.example templates AND the per-install config.<env>
# files checked in. config is NOT secret (domain, cluster name, admin email, host
# prefixes, channels) — it is part of the install branch's reproducible definition.
# Real SECRETS live in secrets/ and stay ignored (below).
configs/*
!configs/*.example
!configs/config.dev
!configs/config.test
!configs/config.prod
# mail-dns.<env>.conf — the mail-DNS publisher's declarative config (sender
# domains, DKIM policy). Public DNS facts, no secrets — versioned per install
# branch exactly like config.<env>. The sender domains are an installation's
# registrable mail apexes, NOT the cluster FQDN, so the domain stamp never
# rewrites them; each install branch carries its own file, master carries none (the
# publisher synthesises the cluster's own domain when no file exists).
!configs/mail-dns.dev.conf
!configs/mail-dns.test.conf
!configs/mail-dns.prod.conf

# secrets/ — consolidated home for ALL secrets: the
# hand-authored Vault-seed inputs (secrets.<env>, secrets.<env>.pub.txt) AND the
# generated credential files ({vault,argocd,kube,idp}-<env>.txt). Keep ONLY the
# secrets.example template checked in; ignore every real secret.
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example

# Belt-and-suspenders: never commit per-env SECRET / credential files even if
# they show up outside the secrets/ directory. (config.<env> is NOT listed here —
# it carries no secrets and is versionable, see the configs/ note above.)
secrets.dev
secrets.test
secrets.prod
secrets.dev.pub.txt
secrets.test.pub.txt
secrets.prod.pub.txt
vault-*.txt
argocd-*.txt
kube-*.txt
idp-*.txt

# Helm dependency build artefacts — `helm dependency build` populates
# `charts/` and `Chart.lock` under each app, but ArgoCD does its own
# dependency fetch when rendering, so tracking these would only bloat the
# repo and cause version drift when Chart.yaml is bumped without a re-build.
apps/*/charts/
apps/*/Chart.lock

# What `dart pub get` writes for the gate package under tools/. It holds ABSOLUTE paths into the
# machine it was resolved on, so it says nothing to any other machine and a copy of it would make
# the analyzer resolve packages that are not there. tools/pubspec.lock is NOT ignored — the gate is
# an application, and every machine that runs it resolves the versions the developer did.
**/.dart_tool/

# NOTE: secrets.enc (the GPG-AES256 encrypted backup of every secret) is
# intentionally NOT ignored — it is COMMITTED to the remote as the off-site,
# encrypted recovery copy.

# Node app sources bundled in this repo (any future in-repo app)
# — never commit dependencies or build output, wherever they sit.
**/node_modules/
*.log

# Temp files
*.tmp
/tmp/

# The compiled binary that gets copied to a machine. It is built in the plugin repository,
# simetrixch/ansiwise-plugins, and dropped in here, so it is an artifact this
# repository carries rather than one it produces.
/bin/*
!/bin/.gitkeep

# Agent instructions. Loaded from disk by whichever harness opens this repository, and never
# tracked: they are ours, and this repository is meant to be cloned and used by anybody.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
